OpenNCALayer is an independent reimplementation of the NCALayer protocol and of the
operations behind it. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the National Certification
Authority of the Republic of Kazakhstan. "NCALayer" and "Kalkan" are used only to describe
compatibility.

src/streebog_secret.rs and src/streebog_secret/consts.rs are derived from the RustCrypto
`streebog` 0.11.0 crate (https://github.com/RustCrypto/hashes, commit
b5051e5a5e7dc86a6c27c1ec7a390744ebcfb97a), Copyright (c) 2016-2026 The RustCrypto Project
Developers and Copyright (c) 2016 Artyom Pavlov, distributed under the MIT or Apache-2.0
licenses and used here under Apache-2.0. consts.rs is a verbatim copy. streebog_secret.rs is
modified for secret input: constant-time selection of the LPS table words (the `subtle`
crate), compression temporaries in one workspace wiped after every block, the state in one
heap allocation made before any input and wiped as soon as the digest is written. It was
first kept in a fork (https://github.com/arynyklas/hashes, branch
`openncalayer/streebog-0.11.0`). src/secret_hmac.rs is our own RFC 2104 HMAC over it. Public
document hashing uses the unmodified crates.io `streebog`.
